---
title: Haloumi Loaf
course: Bread
locale: en
difficulty: Medium
---

> Alternative: Substitute chopped olives for some or all of the haloumi

In a large bowl mix together the @plain flour{500%g}, @dried fast-acting yeast{7%g}(1 sachet), @salt{0.5%tsp} and @caster sugar{0.5%tsp}. Add the @water{400%ml} and half the @olive oil{125%ml} to form a thick batter.

Add the @onion{0.5}(finely chopped), @haloumi{450%g}(cut into 1 cm cubes), and @dried mint{1%tbsp} and mix well.

Use the remaining olive oil to heavily grease a #900 g loaf tin{}. Place the mixture into the tin and spread it out evenly. Cover with a damp cloth and leave it to rise in a warm place for about 2 to ~{3%hours}, until doubled in size.

Preheat the oven to 190°C.

Place the risen loaf in the oven for around ~{45%minutes}, or until golden brown and a lovely crust has formed. A skewer inserted into the centre should come out clean. Leave to cool in the tin for ~{10%minutes}. Use a palette knife to separate the loaf from the edges of the tin, and then turn out gently onto a wire rack to cool completely.